{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1295288-request-for-help-psp-purview-design","id":1295288,"title":"Request for help: PSP Purview design","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-09T05:33:41-08:00","id":1295288,"title":"Request for help: PSP Purview design","content":"Hello, it's been a long time. I just read through the Hero 2e book and I like a lot of what's been done. Now, I used to go by the name &quot;ptah1888&quot; and many years ago, my brother (pashupatastra) and I worked hard doing research and writing and created a fan-based pantheon for Scion (1e). This was the Atua (<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1-ipnmha6lHKmJ6LUNaUoFrhxY1Nacl6m\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=1-i...UoFrhxY1Nacl6m</a>). I would like to begin converting the pantheon to 2e, but I need help working with the PSP, Mana. I flt it was very clunky in my original form. Additionally, some of the powers granted are now covered by the Marvels mechanic. So, I would like advice/help/suggestions for making Atua. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24048-inari_okami","name":"Inari_Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24048_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T06:50:49-08:00","id":1295303,"title":"","content":"First off, I need to say Thank you very much for both of you. I am a great fan of your work. I found your fan-based pantheon a long time ago when I played Scion 1ed, and I loved it. Even convinced a friend of mine to play as an Atuan (hope it is how it spelled) Scion, but as the game never happened, he never played, and was sad when we would need to wait before trying this idea on 2ed.<br /> <br /> Second off, I just read it and, if I may give my (very initial) thoughts about it:<br /> <br /> -&gt; Keep the Mana Purview. It fits even better now than on 1ed, as the PSP are much more focused on the uniqueness of each pantheon and cosmology, and Mana and the Tapus are very uniquely Atua. Unlike the Greek or Norse ones, I dont think it need a hard rewrite, specially concept wise. Also, the breaking of the Tapu inflicts Complications for minor, Conditions for Major and Severe.<br /> <br /> -&gt; For the innate power, the first level (Know Tapu) fits quite well, just give less information about who placed it if it is not a mundane or trivial entity (just &quot;it is a God&quot; or &quot;a Scion&quot;, but not legend ratings or name, but is okay if it was put by an official of Hawain government, lets say.) and take away the part in which you spent Legend. I think it might be overstepping the power of the PSP if it reaches into some others Pantheon PSP.<br /> //Maybe add that the Scion can perceive social norms and taboos from whatever society he is in, if it feels this Innate power is too bare.<br /> <br /> -&gt; Declare Lesser Tapu is a must for the Spent Legend Boon for the PSP. The Scion can declare a tapu under a location or item. Anyone who offends this Tapu suffers a level 2 complication in all his actions. I dont think the &quot;make himself immune&quot; part is very thematic, but if so allow to put specific permissions on the Tapu to allow some liberty (for example, nobody can enter this area, except those who dress in red&quot;). I am not sure if it is how Tapus work on the Atua cosmology/religion, but could seems more thematic with the idea of divine law. I think it fits best for a &quot;Spent Legend&quot; than Imbue because it is more permanent, and if wisely used, can affect literally dozens of enemies.<br /> <br /> -&gt; For the Imbue Legend Boon, a mix of Warriors Mana and Heroes Mana, basically allowing the Scion to, by expanding and controlling his Mana to command certain objects of natural or non-natural origin to give then an appropriated aprimorament (like +2 on attacks from a weapon, or +2 on knowledge from books) or do specific actions (like commanding rocks to move, pools to dry, or cell phones to not work).<br /> <br /> Those are just some ideas I had revisiting your wonderful material. It is quite still initial, but I hope it helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 03-09-2019, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T09:21:02-08:00","id":1295328,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your kind words! I appreciate hearing your suggestions and find them quite suitable. I will work on writing hem up and see about testing them and ironing those out. Of course, any further suggestions (form anyone) are welcome. <br /> <br /> Another trouble I am having is trying to find good sources to reference for the traditional Maori religion in the modern world. If anyone knows anything that they may direct my attention to, they would have my thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24048-inari_okami","name":"Inari_Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24048_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}